113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 51 0 R
/T (For every assignment, the explanation layer compares the chosen partner with the alternatives on the quantities that drive the decision: estimated travel time, risk score and workload. It then produces a short reason in plain language, such as lower travel time, reduced risk or better workload balance. Because the reward is built from named components, the contribution of each component to the chosen action can be reported directly, and feature-attribution methods such as SHAP [9] and LIME [10] can be applied to the neural network when a finer explanation is needed.)
/E (For every assignment, the explanation layer compares the chosen partner with the alternatives on the quantities that drive the decision: estimated travel time, risk score and workload. It then produces a short reason in plain language, such as lower travel time, reduced risk or better workload balance. Because the reward is built from named components, the contribution of each component to the chosen action can be reported directly, and feature-attribution methods such as SHAP [9] and LIME [10] can be applied to the neural network when a finer explanation is needed.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
114 0 obj
<<
