130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 52 0 R
/T (The expected advantage of SmartRoute AI is that the agent can adapt as traffic and demand change, whereas a snapshot method must recompute from scratch, and that risk and workload are considered together with time and distance. The explanation layer lets a dispatcher see why a partner was chosen, which supports trust and makes it easier to find problems with the learned policy.)
/E (The expected advantage of SmartRoute AI is that the agent can adapt as traffic and demand change, whereas a snapshot method must recompute from scratch, and that risk and workload are considered together with time and distance. The explanation layer lets a dispatcher see why a partner was chosen, which supports trust and makes it easier to find problems with the learned policy.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 52 0 R
/T (Several limitations must be kept in view. The simulator is only an approximation of real traffic and order patterns, so results may change on real data. The reward weights affect the behaviour of the agent and need careful tuning. A learned policy offers no guarantee of optimality, which is why the Hungarian baseline is retained for comparison. These points will be examined during the experiments.)
/E (Several limitations must be kept in view. The simulator is only an approximation of real traffic and order patterns, so results may change on real data. The reward weights affect the behaviour of the agent and need careful tuning. A learned policy offers no guarantee of optimality, which is why the Hungarian baseline is retained for comparison. These points will be examined during the experiments.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [13]
>>
