314 0 obj
<<
/Title (Classical assignment methods, such as the Hungarian Algorithm [2], find an optimal one-to-one matching for a fixed cost matrix. In practice, however, orders arrive over time and traffic conditions change, so a matching computed on a snapshot can become poor within minutes. Reinforcement learning offers a different approach in which an agent learns an assignment policy from experience in a changing environment [3], [4]. This paper proposes SmartRoute AI, a DRL framework that adds two features often missing from learned dispatchers: explicit consideration of operational risk and a layer that explains each assignment in plain language.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 221 0 R
/Prev 273 0 R
/Next 315 0 R
>>
endobj
315 0 obj
<<
