384 0 obj
<<
/Title (The assignment problem is modelled as a Markov decision process. At each decision step t, the state st describes the pending orders \(location, deadline and priority\), each partner \(position, current load and availability\) and the traffic conditions together with estimated distance and travel time. The action at assigns a pending order to an available partner. After the action is executed in the environment, the agent receives a reward rt and the environment moves to the next state. The agent learns a policy that maximises the expected cumulative reward.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 276 0 R
/Prev 375 0 R
/Next 393 0 R
>>
endobj
